s, ..., 'all' = the full transitive closure", "type": "string"}, "dry-run": {"default": false, "description": "Plan only: report the shards and reuse decisions, start no checks", "type": "boolean"}, "max-parallel": {"default": "", "description": "Shards to run concurrently, and so the wave size the plan cuts: set it to the concurrency the account really has, never more (GitHub queues past its own limit anyway)", "type": "string"}, "not-cran": {"default": false, "description": "Run the tests CRAN skips: sets NOT_CRAN=true, so skip_on_cran() does not skip (slower, noisier, and includes packages' own spelling tests)", "type": "boolean"}, "packages": {"default": "", "description": "Packages to check (comma/space separated), or 'broken' to take what the committed revdep/ report lists as broken or failed; default: all reverse dependencies", "type": "string"}, "part": {"default": "", "description": "Check one G-th of the reverse dependencies, as 'i/G'; for a set too big for one run (the plan says when, and with which G)", "type": "string"}, "r-version": {"default": "4.6.1", "description": "R version the checks run under: an explicit version like 4.6.1 (the pinned default -- at least one reverse dependency needs R-release), or 'oldrel'/'release' to resolve at run time.", "type": "string"}, "ref": {"default": "", "description": "Branch, tag, or commit SHA to check; default: the dispatched ref", "type": "string"}, "refresh-baseline": {"default": false, "description": "Offer no stored old results as second opinions (the old half always runs fresh either way)", "type": "boolean"}, "retry-run": {"default": "", "description": "Run id of an earlier revdep4 run; re-check only its not-ok packages", "type": "string"}, "shard-budget-minutes": {"default": "", "description": "Check-time target per shard; smaller buys wall clock with more shards, up to one wave of max-parallel", "type": "string"}, "which": {"default": "strong", "description": "Which reverse dependencies to enumerate", "options": ["strong", "most"], "type": "choice"}, "workers": {"default": "", "description": "Packages checked concurrently per shard by the queue (one heavy lane, the rest light); default: the runner's core count", "type": "string"}}}}}, {"has_build_test_lint_hint": true, "jobs": ["setup", "linux-containers", "other-platforms"], "path": ".github/workflows/rhub.yaml", "review": ["SECRET_REFERENCE"], "triggers": {"push": {"branches": ["cran-*"]}, "workflow_dispatch": {"inputs": {"config": {"default": "", "description": "Comma-separated list of R-hub platforms to use. Empty uses the package's platforms, see the top of rhub.yaml. Full list: https://r-hub.github.io/containers/", "type": "string"}, "id": {"description": "Unique ID. You can leave this empty.", "type": "string"}, "name": {"description": "Run name. You can leave this empty.", "type": "string"}}}}}]}
